  "synthesis": {
    "body": "RETIRED 2026-09-17 -- the behaviour this recorded no longer ships; kept for the generalisable half. lint-contract-item-alignment's stale-assertion rule used to execute only when --since supplied a base revision. Without one every run printed '0 finding(s) ... 1 partial (rules with no input: stale-assertion (no --since))', which scans as green; across three spec-review rounds that line was read past about ten times while the same defect was found by hand twice, and supplying --since then flagged seven criteria whose plan assertions had not followed their rewording. The rule now resolves its own base and every no-input entry names the input it lacked. What survives the fix: treat any 'partial (rules with no input)' entry as an un-run rule and supply its input, rather than reading the finding count alone. A rule whose input is optional is a rule that does not run.",
    "kind": "gotcha"
  },
  "title": "A lint rule reported as 'partial' did not run, and the summary still reads as a pass",
  "topic_key": "a-lint-rule-reported-as-partial-did-not-run"
}
